  "conclusion": "All four delivered latency excursions coincide with severe PL1-associated GPU frequency reductions while the GT remains awake. They are dominated by backend graph wall time rather than CPU work, model rebuild, source read, overlap or ready queue delay. The trigger inside firmware/platform power management versus driver scheduling is not established.",
  "evidence_limits": [
    "This first trial did not sustain continuous UI frame notifications; raw status ok is preserved but it does not fulfill the requested full-hour audio/UI validation. All misses overlap bins with nonzero UI frame counts after activity returned in bin30, but minute totals do not establish exact per-hop render concurrency.",
    "EPP and firmware profile are performance in every workload host snapshot; parent policy holds/monitor metadata remain separate evidence.",
    "RC6 changes 0/1/0/0 ms and no runtime-suspended time support awake-GT behavior during sampled native interiors, not exact hardware execution boundaries.",
    "Memory PSI/swap/reclaim signatures do not support multi-second memory pressure as the common explanation. Zero native faults alone would not exclude kernel GEM backing pressure; events at unsampled edges remain possible.",
    "PL1 also occurs on good requests and is not an actual power-watt measurement. RAPL energy access was denied. Which limit or firmware response triggered the severe reduction remains unknown.",
    "No graphics reset/hang/preempt entry was found in the bounded accessible journal. Root-only i915 error-state/tracefs data remain unavailable; negative journal evidence cannot prove absence.",
    "No Mesa GPU trace was configured for this run. Recurrence means prior Mesa tracing is not a necessary condition, but host sampling and the usual desktop remain observational overhead.",
    "Sampling read duration max 180.221 ms and gap max 682.487 ms are below multi-second stall duration; they do not establish zero observer influence.",
    "Do not change preemption timeouts, raise power limits, force priority, or ship INTEL_DEBUG synchronization on this evidence. A controlled full-hour balanced comparison with equivalent continuous UI load would be a narrower future policy test after valid full-load performance replication."
  ]
